    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters July 27th with a high-upside lineup, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (83.49) and **James Wood** (76.28), our two most potent weapons today. **Corbin Carroll** draws an elite matchup against Keller, benefiting from a 10% boost for his leadoff spot and favorable platoon dynamics against the righty; his ability to weaponize SB makes him our essential engine today. **James Wood** is similarly positioned to exploit a soft 5.89 xERA starter, bolstered by an elite 0.420 xwOBA and a generous 10% leadoff cushion. **Jose Caballero** (76.02) rounds out our elite tier, as his 13% platoon edge against the lefty Schultz mitigates his lower batting order position, making him a high-efficiency play for our pursuit of SB and counting stats.\n\nThe optimization process required a nuanced decision at the utility spot, where **Isaac Paredes** (67.28) narrowly edged out our depth options to secure the start. While **Tyler Soderstrom** (55.04) carries a favorable park factor, his 6% platoon penalty against a lefty dampened his floor, keeping him in the lineup but lower than the rest of our core. We are monitoring **Austin Riley** (54.19) closely, as he remains a marginal start; despite his base projection, the 31% rain risk in his matchup and a minor negative adjustment for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time create a volatile scenario that could necessitate a late swap if lineups shift. With **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined, our depth is thin, but we remain confident in the current configuration of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Cole Young**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Zach McKinstry** to maintain our efficiency across the 5x5 categories.",
